{"id": "xfiji", "name": "Colo-i-Suva Forest Reserve", "short": "Colo-i-Suva", "place": "Viti Levu, Fiji", "lat": -18.05, "lon": 178.45, "side": "r", "cont": "Oceania", "country": "Fiji", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Fig trees, fruit bats and a rare Fijian rainforest above Suva.", "tip": {"id": "ficus", "title": "Lose the fig trees", "text": "Figs feed bats, pigeons, parrots and bulbuls. Set Fig trees to -100% and watch the fruit eaters, then the goshawk above them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Colo-i-Suva Forest Reserve", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colo-i-Suva_Forest_Reserve"}, {"title": "National Parks: Colo-i-Suva Forest Park", "url": "https://national-parks.org/fiji/colo-i-suva-forest-park/"}, {"title": "Living Dreams: Birds of Colo-i-Suva", "url": "https://www.livingdreams.tv/fiji/birds-of-colo-i-suva-forest-park"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Fiji goshawk", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiji_goshawk"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Collared lory", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collared_lory"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Vanikoro flycatcher", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanikoro_flycatcher"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Colo-i-Suva Forest Reserve", "icon": "aspen", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.15, "desc": "Light reaching the canopy and the gaps along streams drives growth in this warm, wet forest."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "heavy rainfall", "xh": 0.38, "desc": "The Suva side of Viti Levu is very wet, which keeps the forest green and its creeks running."}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "forest soil", "xh": 0.6, "desc": "Leaf litter and decaying wood build the soil that the rainforest plants root in."}, {"id": "creek", "sp": "waisila creek", "xh": 0.82},